# DJ Library Tools

Cross-platform Python CLI to manage the **Master** DJ music library on NAS and sync to Serato/Rekordbox. Documented in README.md and AGENT_HANDOFF.md.

Source of truth: AGENT_HANDOFF.md, TEST_PLAN.md, TECH_DEBT.md, RISKS.md; `.cursor/skills/` (DEV_GUIDE, TEST_TDD, tester, green-and-clean, context-bootstrapper, session-summarizer, code-reviewer, tech-debt-evaluator, github-feature-workflow).

**Operating model:** Use green-and-clean for scope discipline; use context-bootstrapper when starting/resuming; use session-summarizer when handing off.

**TDD:** Read TEST_TDD.md and tester skill first; Tier 1 is `python -m pytest -q`. Add failing tests before new production logic in `lib/`.

**Merge-ready:** `python -m pytest -q` (documented in AGENT_HANDOFF.md). Run before commit on behavior changes.

**Branches / push:** Follow `.cursor/skills/github-feature-workflow/SKILL.md` and AGENT_HANDOFF.md → Git workflow.

**Safety:** Master is the single source of truth. Never delete from Master without explicit user approval.

**Handoff:** When the user wants a handoff, run code review, tech debt evaluation, and pytest; record in the handoff note. See `.cursor/rules/handoff-checklist.mdc`.
